Why Miranda Lambert Didn&#8217;t Want to Advise Ella Langley After &#8216;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8217; Hit Big: &#8216;You Might Need to Call Taylor&nbsp;Swift&#8217;

Miranda Lambert Keeps Her Top 10 Streak Cooking With ‘Crisco’&nbsp;Debut

Miranda Lambert on Blending Country and Disco on Her New Album: &#8216;Dolly’s All Over&nbsp;This&#8217;

Lambert took to Instagram to share a series of photos and videos for McLoughlin&#8217;s 35th birthday on Wednesday (Oct. 14), alongside the caption: &#8220;Happy Birthday @brendanjmcloughlin. 35 looks good on you! Well everything looks good on you but that smile is my favorite ! I love you!&#8221;

In addition to pics of McLoughlin poolside, wearing cowboy boots on his hands, holding up Whataburger bags, fishing or riding a jet ski, Lambert also shared a few videos. There&#8217;s the one that paints a pretty clear picture of their life in rural Tennessee, showing McLoughlin driving down a country road while Lambert sits shotgun with her feet propped on the windowsill and their dog in the backseat. Then there&#8217;s one in which McLoughlin can be seen sweetly lacing Lambert&#8217;s pink low-top Jordans.

But the best video is the final one, which was shot in a hotel bathroom, with Lambert serenading her husband as he gets ready for a night out in Sin City.

&#8220;He&#8217;s in Vegas I can tell by the way he wants to leave the room,&#8221; Lambert sings in her unmistakable twang, set to the tune of the &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8221; chorus. &#8220;Judging by the smile that&#8217;s written on his face, he&#8217;s got a lot to lose.&#8221; (McLoughlin laughs as he admits to his wife, &#8220;That&#8217;s true!&#8221;) Lambert keeps singing to finish up the chorus: &#8220;It doesn&#8217;t take a crystal ball to see, Brendan&#8217;s gonna gamble until he&#8217;s/ Drinkin&#8217; Jack all by himself, he&#8217;s in Vegas I can tell.&#8221;

Lambert is all too familiar with &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas,&#8221; as she co-wrote and co-produced the song alongside Langley, as well as co-writers Luke Dick and JoyBeth Taylor and co-producer Ben West. The song has since rewritten the Hot 100 record book, spending 24 weeks atop the chart and surpassing the previous benchmark set by Mariah Carey&#8217;s &#8220;All I Want for Christmas Is You&#8221; with 22 weeks at No. 1.

McLoughlin and Lambert started dating in November 2018 before getting married only a few months later in January 2019 in Tennessee. In addition to her work with Langley, Lambert put out her 10th solo album Crisco on Oct. 2, which debuts at No. 4 on the Top Country Albums chart this week.

